## 2026-09-24T21:50:00Z session — statbel.fgov.be refuses a non-browser client
curl https://statbel.fgov.be/sites/default/files/Over_Statbel_FR/Nomenclaturen/REFNIS_2025.csv → 200 with an HTML bot challenge (`/TSPD/?type=25`), no CSV
- resolved: the register comes from NGI's `georef-belgium-municipality` (year 2025, 565 communes) on public.opendatasoft.com, which carries the same NIS codes; scripts/communes/build.ts names it.
- rule: statbel.fgov.be answers scripts with a bot challenge; regenerate the commune register from NGI's dataset on public.opendatasoft.com (scripts/communes/build.ts), never from Statbel.

## 2026-09-24T22:00:00Z session — NGI's postcode table misplaces postcodes
scripts/communes/build.ts: Error: communes with no postcode: Mol, Trooz, Enghien (2400 carries Dessel's area, one commune per postcode)
- resolved: postcodes are bpost's list (jief/zipcode-belgium) placed by point into the 2025 communes, with bpost's province ranges and a 20 km outlier rule; every commune now has a postcode and the build fails loudly otherwise.

## 2026-09-24T22:40:00Z ci Vercel — preview build fails in `drizzle-kit migrate` after merging main
Error: Command "npm run vercel-build" exited with 1 (applying migrations: 0003_onboarding_professionnelle hit types created by this run's pre-merge 0002, still recorded on preview/claude/quirky-cannon-ta3dag)
- resolved: main's 0002_family_profiles took the number this run had used; the migration was regenerated as 0003 on the merged tree, and the PR's preview branch (empty) had the pre-merge objects and their __drizzle_migrations row dropped (operator-approved), then the build re-applied 0002 and 0003.
- rule: when a merge of main renumbers this branch's Drizzle migration, the PR's Neon preview branch still holds the old one: drop its objects and its __drizzle_migrations row (or reset the branch from its parent) before trusting the next preview build.
